    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36845" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pŏlītĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		1. polio, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a smoothing</i>, <i>a furbishing</i>,
				<i>polishing.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b> (post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">speculi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr. 7,
					3</span></i>
			.—Of <i>smoothing</i> or <i>plastering</i> a wall, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 7,
			4</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>an improving</i>,
				<i>cultivating</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">agrorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 136</span></i>
			.</div>
